    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **269 tests, 0 failures**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the sequential membership number feature for newly created owners, following the OfficeFloor function-injection architecture.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a readOnly `membershipNumber` (integer/int32) property to the `Owner` response schema. This regenerates `OwnerDto` (with the JSON field) and the MapStruct `OwnerMapperImpl` (which now auto-maps `membershipNumber` by name).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient Integer membershipNumber` field with getter/setter. It's transient because the number is derived/computed, not a persisted column, so it stays out of the DB schema while flowing through the mapper into the response.\n\n3. **`AssignMembershipNumber.java`** (new function step) \u2014 computes `ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1` and sets it on the owner (mutating the `@Val Owner` in place), i.e. one more than the current number of owners.\n\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `assignMembershipNumber` step into the pipeline between `checkDuplicateEmail` and `save` (under `govern: [ transaction ]`), so the number is assigned against the existing count before the new owner is persisted, then `RespondWithOwnerCreated` maps it into the 201 response.\n\n5. **Test** \u2014 added `createOwnerAssignsSequentialMembershipNumber`, asserting the response's `$.membershipNumber` equals the pre-existing owner count + 1.\n\nThe number is populated on the creation response; on GET/list it's naturally null since it isn't persisted, consistent with the spec which only requires it on creation.",
